! ax4b_4_fp_18bit.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148 (1248, "INDEX
! MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113: "TEST4. CHECK FLOATING POINT,
! 18 BITS, MODIFICATION."), TEST 4 "18 BIT FLOATING POINT
! MODIFICATION":
!
!   PDF p.141  010715.40-010736.00  the whole block
!   PDF p.153  011351.00-011363.00  148K24, 148XW2, 148XW3
!   PDF p.153  011372.00            148ER1
!   PDF p.191  013071.00            BIT13
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 and 300 dpi; checked row
! for row by tests/verify_ax4b_4_fp_18bit_listing.py (39 rows, 7
! symbols).
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  A floating-point address is 18
! bits; the index value's bits 18-23 must not reach it.
!   148ER1's count is 0 ("PREVIOUS FP FAILURE PROHIBITS RUNNING THIS
!   TEST" otherwise), so BXCZ goes to I4832.
!   X1 := BIT13+.32 (value 13071.40, bit 18 set)
!   L(N),0($X1)     0.00 61   loads BIT13 NORMALIZED; KV,$X1,BIT13 /
!                   BXH then requires $L's first 24 bits to EXCEED
!                   BIT13's 20.00 ("GATING BIT 18 SPURIOUSLY" otherwise).
!                   Worked by hand, not pinned (X1 is reloaded after):
!                   the one fraction bit (13) moves to bit 12 and the
!                   exponent becomes -1, so they read 34.00.  An
!                   unnormalized load would read exactly 20.00.
!   X1 := 148K24+.63 (value 11351.77, bits 18-23 all set)
!   L(U),0($X1)     0.40 61   loads 148K24 unnormalized; KV and KC
!                   compare $L's value and count fields with 148K24's
!                   ("GATING SOME OF 19-23 SPUR." otherwise).
! The exit B,$+1.0 / BD,I4832 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW is the routine's
! usual one.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44,
!     read in the page image), so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the
!     error entry on a failure.
!   * IC248, BIT20 and I4833 (TEST 5A's entry, "B,I4833 -TERMINATE.")
!     are SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10),
!     "V+,$X13,BIT20" (13100.32 B0) and "B,I4833" (10736.50 00); they
!     are reached only on the 148ER1 path or after B,SSW.
!   * TEST 4's first row has no label; END names its printed location,
!     (8)10715.40, rather than adding one.
!   * Notation only: the page's "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")";
!     the label glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..),
!     as for every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing
!     else changed.
!
! RESULT ON THE MODEL, 2026-11-18 (a57832f + this deck): PASSES -- halts
! at SSW (PC 1410), SEN = 0, $X1 = 148K24's word (0x29CBBE029CB80000:
! L(U) left the whole word in $L, value and count).  CYCLES 309 is MODEL
! BEHAVIOUR; no time is printed.  IBM's listing and the model AGREE.
!
! INJECTIONS, each in a scratch copy of bsv/, OBSERVED for this deck:
!   FP normalization off (normalized = False) -> FAIL halt, SEN 010725.00:
!     the L(N) check, "GATING BIT 18 SPURIOUSLY.", CYCLES 182.
!   effAddr18 returns ea[23:6] + ea[5] (bit 18 rounds up) -> FAIL halt, SEN
!     010725.00, the same L(N) check (BIT13+.32 reads BIT13's successor),
!     CYCLES 182.  Predicted 010732.40 (the L(U) check); it failed earlier.
!   NOT SHOWN: no injection measured here reaches the second half (L(U)
!     through 148XW3, "GATING SOME OF 19-23 SPUR."); both stop at L(N).
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model, the pins below (PASS, SEN = 0).
!   Each built in a scratch copy of bsv/ and restored (cmp IDENTICAL).
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
! The addresses are the ones this listing prints for them (SIC,SEN
! "1310.00 80", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80", B,SSW
! "1301.10 00"), the same as routine 148's; what is AT them is SSIP's,
! which this file replaces with halts, as ax4b_148_immediate_indexed does.
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! IC248, BIT20 and I4833 (TEST 5A's entry): SYN from the printed
! addresses of "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10), "V+,$X13,BIT20" (13100.32
! B0) and "B,I4833" (10736.50 00).  The rows that name them are reached
! only on the "PREVIOUS FP FAILURE" path or after B,SSW, never here.
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
BIT20   SYN, (8)13100.0
I4833   SYN, (8)10736.40
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.141, 010715.40-010736.00 (no printed page number on the sheet)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)10715.40
        LX,  $X1, I48ER1              ! -TEST 4, 18 BIT FLOATING
        BXCZ, I4832                   ! -POINT MODIFICATION.
        SIC, SEN                      ! -PREVIOUS FP FAILURE PROHIBITS
        B,   SERS                     ! -RUNNING THIS TEST.
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        V+,  $X13, BIT20
        SX,  $X13, IC248
        B,   I4833                    ! -TERMINATE.
!
I4832   LX,  $X1, I48XW2
        L(N), 0($X1)
        LX,  $X1, $L
        KV,  $X1, BIT13
        BXH, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN
        B,   SERS                     ! -GATING BIT 18 SPURIOUSLY.
        B,   I48321
!
        LX,  $X1, I48XW3
        L(U), 0($X1)
        LX,  $X1, $L
        KV,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.0
        B,   $+1.32
        KC,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B,   SERS                     ! -GATING SOME OF 19-23 SPUR.
!
I48321  B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4832
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        V+,  $X13, BIT20
        SX,  $X13, IC248
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.153, 011351.00-011372.00: the constants TEST 4 reads
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)11351.0
I48K24  XW,  (8)123456.76, (8)123456, 0
        SLC, (8)11362.0
I48XW2  XW,  BIT13+.32, 0, 0
I48XW3  XW,  I48K24+.63, 0, 0
        SLC, (8)11372.0
I48ER1  XW,  0, 0, 0                  ! -V I SELN, C FP, R VFL.
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.191, 013071.00: BIT13, the word L(N) loads
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)13071.0
BIT13   XW,  (8)20.00, 0, 0
        END, (8)10715.40                ! TEST 4 has no label: its first row
